# Assignment 2 – Implementing Operator Overloads for Square Matrices

## Overview
This project implements operator overloading for square matrices using a custom `SquareMat` class in C++.
It supports arithmetic, comparison, and matrix-specific operations (like transpose and determinant).
The project includes unit tests using the **doctest** framework and checks for memory leaks using **Valgrind**.

As part of this assignment, the **Rule of Three** is implemented — including a custom copy constructor, assignment operator, and destructor — to ensure proper memory management and avoid shallow copies.

---

## Features
- Dynamic 2D array allocation for `n x n` matrices
- Safe element access with bounds checking via `mat[i][j]` syntax
- Full suite of arithmetic, comparison, and matrix operators
- Determinant calculation, matrix exponentiation, and transpose
- Unit tests with doctest and memory check with Valgrind

---

## Project Structure

- **SquareMat.h / SquareMat.cpp**
  Implements the `SquareMat` class using a dynamically allocated `double** data`.
  Includes all core functionality and overloaded operators.

- **RowProxy (Inner Class)**
  Allows double-indexing (`mat[i][j]`) with bounds checking.
  Supports both const and non-const access. Throws `std::invalid_argument` on invalid indices.

- **main.cpp**
  Demonstrates usage of all overloaded operators.

- **Test.cpp**
  Unit tests written using the [doctest](https://github.com/doctest/doctest) framework.

- **Makefile**
  Automates compilation, testing, memory checking, and cleanup.

