## Implemented Operators

### Arithmetic Operators
- `+`, `-`: Element-wise addition or subtraction between matrices of the same size
- `*`: Matrix multiplication or scalar multiplication
- `/`: Scalar division (each element divided by a non-zero scalar)
- `%`:
  - `mat % scalar`: Applies modulo to each element
  - `mat1 % mat2`: Element-wise multiplication (same size required)
- `^`: Matrix exponentiation (positive integer power)

### Unary Operators
- `-`: Negates all matrix elements
- `!`: Computes the determinant
- `~`: Transposes the matrix

### Comparison Operators
- `==`, `!=`: Matrices are equal if the **sum of their elements** is equal
- `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`: Based on the **sum of elements** in each matrix

### Increment/Decrement
- `++`, `--`: Increments or decrements each element by 1 (both pre and post)

### Assignment Operators
- `+=`, `-=`, `*=`, `/=`, `%=`: Perform the operation and update in-place

### Element Access
- `mat[i][j]`: Accesses elements with full bounds checking

### Output Stream
- `<<`: Prints the matrix in a readable format

